#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286824 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "947eb2bb-0443-5740-9d45-847c70877270" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Surface Area of a Polyhedron Given Some Lengths"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "534c30cd-fb91-5d73-a130-bbcbb6b18e26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "132\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286826} {:answer/id #uuid "1a4b29d0-df4c-5668-bfcf-e3143e442641" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "116\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286827} {:answer/id #uuid "80a20c95-701b-5f59-894b-467ccfcb4639" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "126\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286828} {:answer/id #uuid "d2911c93-110c-5b4a-bbd6-1bf9a421d5a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "142\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286829} {:answer/id #uuid "f1828f98-4786-5226-a063-0b73d2757f28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "96\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286830}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "534c30cd-fb91-5d73-a130-bbcbb6b18e26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "132\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286826} :answer-field/id #uuid "a431bdc3-b162-55af-82be-915961c75955" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286825}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2a7cfcf9-d573-54e4-af00-b3e2f3d9834c" :question/math-academy-id "q-61705" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/assets/4b0c67b6a8c18b4f05198c209dae8cb960c9bfdcfc8310d0f59ee7a717e68f41.png)\n\nAssuming that all side faces have the same height of $8\\,\\text{cm}$, find the total surface area of the square pyramid above using its net." :question/worked-solution "The net of our pyramid is the following.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/assets/1fc39646f2b26116f97bc5340b0a7211911ba64ae59e4ce652bf13018fb7ef33.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that the base of the pyramid is a square with a side equal to $6\\,\\text{cm}.$ Hence:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the square}=6\\times 6=36\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\n$$\n\n \n\nEach side face of our solid is triangle, where the base is $6\\,\\text{cm}$ and the height is $8\\,\\text{cm}.$ Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the triangle}=\\frac{1}{2}\\times 6\\times 8=24\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the surface area of the pyramid consists of $1$ square (base) and $4$ triangles (side faces). \n\nTherefore, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =(\\text{Area of the square})+4\\times (\\text{Area of the triangle}) \\\\  & =36+4\\times 24 \\\\  & =36+96 \\\\  & =132\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286831 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "947eb2bb-0443-5740-9d45-847c70877270" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Surface Area of a Polyhedron Given Some Lengths"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fb08f65-bdfb-5d0d-8d51-6bcf5c70d142" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "125\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286833} {:answer/id #uuid "31e13b82-dfc0-5253-a9e0-683206ae8f15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "175\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286834} {:answer/id #uuid "0c54a474-6a7e-5848-8a57-b229ac9c8c09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "200\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286835} {:answer/id #uuid "974098d5-4a74-5bc6-8e9f-176b542a656c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "150\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286836} {:answer/id #uuid "cac128f3-1f0f-51cc-a295-f0cf0466b10b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286837}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "974098d5-4a74-5bc6-8e9f-176b542a656c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "150\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286836} :answer-field/id #uuid "b655c15c-1eba-55c7-93bf-48858a513d61" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286832}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e80ccdcb-f8a7-5672-8914-73b42c8ccce6" :question/math-academy-id "q-61907" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/assets/d480892817efecf5ebea6860bece7cbae8127a9840e94ece34f9e83313abd5e5.png)\n\nWhat is the total surface area of the cube above if it is $5\\,\\text{cm}$ long, $5\\,\\text{cm}$ wide, and $5\\,\\text{cm}$ tall?" :question/worked-solution "First, let's consider the net of our plank.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/assets/efca24e18b188363ec3698ff4deaa5d5bd4ec1bdb5075138f925573a407c1f79.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have squares only.\n\nThe squares are $5\\,\\text{cm}$ long and $5\\,\\text{cm}$ high. So, the area of one square is:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the square}=5\\times 5=25\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the surface area of the cube consists of $6$ squares. \n\nTherefore, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =6\\times (\\text{Area of the square}) \\\\  & =6\\times 25 \\\\  & =150\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286838 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "35a19512-4ba7-59c1-ae00-7b8f158264fe" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Surface Area of a Polyhedron Given the Areas of the Faces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "150d41e1-88e6-597c-9822-f7baadc67066" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "390\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286840} {:answer/id #uuid "254e4b31-ec04-5d7e-98c8-a193dbf60d17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "470\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286841} {:answer/id #uuid "dfda0720-c887-56dd-be2c-4c40041ae20f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "370\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286842} {:answer/id #uuid "f96e2017-5817-59ea-8405-c52c86f24ef9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "480\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286843} {:answer/id #uuid "95335036-0d3e-5ad6-9464-d14b33b0cb99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "450\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286844}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "254e4b31-ec04-5d7e-98c8-a193dbf60d17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "470\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286841} :answer-field/id #uuid "5778cc83-438b-5adb-a053-a68a0b7e7e14" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286839}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "874f7685-d103-5726-ba3b-57ef24e4bac6" :question/math-academy-id "q-93262" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/assets/d2fe4346f503215ec6594655cf633ad46b62bc87572339bd1728e6535bef851a.png)\n\nWhat is the total surface area of the rectangular pyramid represented by the net above?" :question/worked-solution "The surface area of our pyramid consists of $1$ square (base) and $4$ triangles (side faces). \n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =1\\times (\\text{Area of the base})+4\\times (\\text{Area of the side}) \\\\  & =1\\times 150+4\\times 80 \\\\  & =150+320 \\\\  & =470\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286845 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1233be4b-7634-5882-9ae5-3200a9da71d8" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Surface Area of a Polyhedron Given the Areas of the Faces: Word Problems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b91af242-7352-528f-8aa4-1c8b71c3a55f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "52\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286847} {:answer/id #uuid "f422fbea-9765-532b-b9ca-c6f898e45522" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "46\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286848} {:answer/id #uuid "dec571db-d2ae-5656-99b9-c8bb6f0de6da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286849} {:answer/id #uuid "eab26e7c-e3c8-5894-9f41-fd9c42d0a241" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "44\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286850} {:answer/id #uuid "964a496d-5548-5d20-ad43-26cb2b140e66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286851}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eab26e7c-e3c8-5894-9f41-fd9c42d0a241" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "44\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286850} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7c555f5-b80c-5954-aed6-442177da0a71" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286846}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d119284d-a155-58d7-994e-d134bc9c1879" :question/math-academy-id "q-93343" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/assets/3d0b6b63883b58ecce92e395380b140b32946a4bb037e1829544539749412af9.png)\n\nLiz deconstructs a lantern and gets the net shown above. In the figure, the areas of two of its faces are shown. What is the total surface area of the lantern?" :question/worked-solution "The net shown corresponds to a triangular pyramid. The surface area of our pyramid consists of $1$ triangle (base) and $3$ triangles (side faces). \n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =1\\times (\\text{Area of the base})+3\\times (\\text{Area of the side}) \\\\  & =1\\times 5+3\\times 13 \\\\  & =5+39 \\\\  & =44\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286852 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1233be4b-7634-5882-9ae5-3200a9da71d8" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Surface Area of a Polyhedron Given the Areas of the Faces: Word Problems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "773c57b3-945f-5976-9a82-2df9e373e851" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "67\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286854} {:answer/id #uuid "2c3fb9d3-3252-57c9-affa-295244d45666" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "59\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286855} {:answer/id #uuid "82af3bb2-3827-5c22-8fcf-ff8b92facb75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "54\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286856} {:answer/id #uuid "dfbb9ed0-fffb-5a91-969a-38395037cd0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286857} {:answer/id #uuid "1cee7620-a974-54bd-b464-183c697c6975" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286858}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "773c57b3-945f-5976-9a82-2df9e373e851" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "67\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286854} :answer-field/id #uuid "65244b1e-c4ce-5466-8884-bbcf56568e37" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286853}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bcc3ddc4-ae0f-5ef4-a719-c3482960a177" :question/math-academy-id "q-93345" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/assets/a8264c635006c74c2d9a7ca4eb3ab8d937ae7b270b4567373d022186c787bbc1.png)\n\nAn artist makes a glass sculpture. In the figure, the areas of some of the faces are displayed in a net of the sculpture. What is the total surface area of the sculpture?" :question/worked-solution "The net shown corresponds to a triangular prism. The surface area of our prism consists of $2$ triangles (base and top) and $3$ rectangles (central and side faces). \n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =2\\times (\\text{Area of the base})+3\\times (\\text{Area of the side faces}) \\\\  & =2\\times 8+3\\times 17 \\\\  & =16+51 \\\\  & =67\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
